src/xlator:
===========

This directory contains the source to the Objective-C translator.
It includes a lex scanner, which can be passed to FSF's flex, or
the UN*X lex program.  There are a few dependencies of these files
on the objc include files, specifically the include files:
        objc/objc.h        objc/release.h

You should modify the 'makefile' to store the executables in your
/bin directory.  The compiler can be built using 16-bit int's or
32-bit int's, it doesn't matter.  The compiler failed when compiled
for a combined 64K code and seg area (small model) under '286 Xenix.

--- brian witt, 18-April-90
